For an integer n \ge 2, if the arithmetic mean of all coefficients in the binomial expansion of (x + y)^{2n-3} is 16, then the distance of the point P(2n-1, n^2-4n) from the line x + y = 8 is:

(A) \sqrt{2}
(B) 2\sqrt{2}
(C) 5\sqrt{2}
(D) 3\sqrt{2}

Consider two vectors \mathbf{u}=3\mathbf{i}-\mathbf{j} and \mathbf{v}=2\mathbf{i}+\mathbf{j}-\lambda\mathbf{k}, \lambda > 0. The angle between them is given by \cos^{-1}\bigl(\tfrac{\sqrt{5}}{2\sqrt{7}}\bigr). Let \mathbf{v}=\mathbf{v}_1+\mathbf{v}_2, where \mathbf{v}_1 is parallel to \mathbf{u} and \mathbf{v}_2 is perpendicular to \mathbf{u}. Then the value of |\mathbf{v}_1|^2 + |\mathbf{v}_2|^2 is:

(A) \tfrac{23}{2}
(B) 14
(C) \tfrac{25}{2}
(D) 10

A box contains 10 pens of which 3 are defective. A sample of 2 pens is drawn at random and let X denote the number of defective pens. Then the variance of X is:

(A) \tfrac{11}{15}
(B) \tfrac{28}{75}
(C) \tfrac{2}{15}
(D) \tfrac{3}{5}

The sum of all values of $\theta \in [0, 2\pi]$ satisfying $2\sin^2 \theta = \cos 2\theta$ and $2\cos^2 \theta = 3\sin \theta$ is:

(A) 4\pi
(B) \frac{5\pi}{6}
(C) \pi
(D) \frac{5}{2}

